WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.880 --> 00:00:05.390
He may have already looked god-like in all
of his DC appearances, but Henry Cavill took

00:00:05.390 --> 00:00:09.820
his workouts to a whole new level in order
to play the lead in Netflix's The Witcher.

00:00:09.820 --> 00:00:13.620
Here's how he got into the best shape of his
life to play Geralt of Rivia.

00:00:14.380 --> 00:00:18.100
To make sure that he was looking as shredded
as humanly possible for his many shirtless

00:00:18.100 --> 00:00:22.000
scenes in The Witcher, Cavill allowed himself
to systematically dehydrate.

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:26.160
Over the course of four days, he would gradually
reduce his fluid intake so that when the time

00:00:26.160 --> 00:00:28.580
came to shoot, he had zero water weight.

00:00:28.580 --> 00:00:31.340
As he explained during an appearance on The
Graham Norton Show,

00:00:31.340 --> 00:00:35.160
"Yeah it gets your, makes your skin really
thin, so it sits on the muscles."

00:00:35.160 --> 00:00:38.920
He goes on to explain the grueling, borderline
masochistic process:

00:00:38.920 --> 00:00:42.820
"On the first day you'll have a liter and
a half, and the second day half a liter, and

00:00:42.820 --> 00:00:45.510
then the third day no water, and then you'll
shoot the fourth."

00:00:45.510 --> 00:00:49.940
Cavill has plenty of experience when it comes
to pushing his body to the limits for a role,

00:00:49.940 --> 00:00:53.360
but this was definitely a tough ask, even
for him.

00:00:53.370 --> 00:00:54.650
The actor even admitted,

00:00:54.650 --> 00:00:58.020
"You're the most miserable person on the planet."

00:00:58.020 --> 00:00:59.340
In fact, he says that,

00:00:59.340 --> 00:01:02.940
"You get to the point on the last day where
you can smell water nearby."

00:01:02.940 --> 00:01:05.220
Well, the results speak for themselves.

00:01:05.220 --> 00:01:09.460
The internet went wild when shots of Geralt
in the bathtub were included in the Witcher trailer.

00:01:10.240 --> 00:01:14.619
Believe it or not, Henry Cavill was once told
that he was too fat to play James Bond.

00:01:14.620 --> 00:01:19.280
The actor was up for the role of 007 in the
period between Pierce Brosnan and Daniel Craig,

00:01:19.280 --> 00:01:21.620
and he received some rather harsh feedback.

00:01:21.620 --> 00:01:23.640
As he explained to Men's Health UK,

00:01:23.640 --> 00:01:27.740
"I remember the director [of Casino Royale],
Martin Campbell, saying, 'Looking a little

00:01:27.740 --> 00:01:28.819
chubby there, Henry.

00:01:28.820 --> 00:01:30.580
I didn't know how to train or diet.

00:01:30.580 --> 00:01:33.719
And I'm glad Martin said something, because
I respond well to truth.

00:01:33.719 --> 00:01:34.990
It helps me get better."

00:01:34.990 --> 00:01:38.940
Cavill learned all about the importance of
training and dieting in the years that followed,

00:01:38.940 --> 00:01:42.840
but it wasn't until he started preparing for
The Witcher that he began to truly appreciate

00:01:42.840 --> 00:01:44.820
what goes into being a bodybuilder.

00:01:44.820 --> 00:01:48.580
In an Instagram post, Cavill revealed that
he'd been reading into the big players of

00:01:48.590 --> 00:01:51.630
the bodybuilding game, and he found himself
in awe of them.

00:01:51.630 --> 00:01:52.679
The caption reads:

00:01:52.679 --> 00:01:56.950
"It's absolutely fascinating to see what they
put themselves through, the drive and mental

00:01:56.950 --> 00:01:59.740
strength required to get to such a place physically.

00:01:59.740 --> 00:02:03.759
Phil Heath in particular has caught my eye
not only for his achievements but also for

00:02:03.759 --> 00:02:07.259
his genuinely humble and informative approach
to his messaging."

00:02:07.260 --> 00:02:11.280
Clearly all of his hard work paid off…but
perhaps that goes without saying.

00:02:11.280 --> 00:02:14.900
"There I go again, just…delivering exposition."

00:02:15.360 --> 00:02:19.980
To get more ripped than ever for The Witcher,
Cavill joined forces with Dave Rienzi, the

00:02:19.990 --> 00:02:23.610
strength and conditioning coach that helps
sculpt some of the biggest bodies in Hollywood.

00:02:23.610 --> 00:02:28.420
In fact, none other than Dwayne Johnson calls
him the "mastermind" behind his fitness regimen.

00:02:28.420 --> 00:02:32.760
Rienzi suggested that Cavill try something
called fasted cardio to get into next-level

00:02:32.760 --> 00:02:34.860
shape for his big Netflix series.

00:02:34.860 --> 00:02:39.220
This essentially means working out when your
body isn't processing or digesting food, which

00:02:39.221 --> 00:02:41.690
is thought to help burn fat at a faster rate.

00:02:41.690 --> 00:02:44.540
So did this turn Henry Cavill into Hangry
Cavill?

00:02:44.540 --> 00:02:45.840
Evidently not.

00:02:45.840 --> 00:02:50.180
Explaining that he starts his day with an
empty-stomach workout, Cavill told Men's Health UK,

00:02:50.180 --> 00:02:53.240
"It's some of the best, or most enjoyable
cardio I've done.

00:02:53.240 --> 00:02:56.060
It's only 20 minutes, so it's not massively
exhausting.

00:02:56.060 --> 00:03:00.040
It's not like doing [high intensity interval
training] which, psychologically, can be quite

00:03:00.040 --> 00:03:00.620
grueling.

00:03:00.620 --> 00:03:06.860
My heart rate's at 125-135bpm, so it has a
really good effect on fat-loss."

00:03:06.860 --> 00:03:10.650
Cavill went on to tell the men's mag that
Rienzi's suggestion helped him reach peak

00:03:10.650 --> 00:03:12.400
fitness for his debut as Geralt.

00:03:12.400 --> 00:03:13.700
The buff Brit revealed,

00:03:13.700 --> 00:03:17.730
"Out of all the things I've done in the past,
I think the fasted cardio stuff is actually

00:03:17.730 --> 00:03:18.730
working best for me.

00:03:18.730 --> 00:03:20.220
I'm in the best shape of my life."

00:03:21.300 --> 00:03:24.780
When Cavill convinced Netflix to let him be
Geralt in The Witcher, he knew exactly what

00:03:24.780 --> 00:03:26.280
he was signing up for.

00:03:26.280 --> 00:03:30.440
In fact, he's reportedly a huge fan of the
source material and relentlessly pursued the

00:03:30.440 --> 00:03:32.510
role when he heard the show was being made.

00:03:32.510 --> 00:03:35.820
The actor was well aware of what the character
called for, and the fact that he was going

00:03:35.820 --> 00:03:39.790
to be doing his own action sequences meant
that his body had to be able to withstand

00:03:39.790 --> 00:03:40.520
the strain.

00:03:40.520 --> 00:03:45.200
To get Cavill where he needed to be, coach
Dave Rienzi introduced some grueling new exercises

00:03:45.210 --> 00:03:46.440
to his workouts.

00:03:46.440 --> 00:03:50.570
In a Men's Health tutorial video, Cavill and
Rienzi explain and demonstrate the killer

00:03:50.570 --> 00:03:51.880
moves they employed.

00:03:51.880 --> 00:03:52.880
Cavill revealed that,

00:03:52.880 --> 00:03:58.460
"For The Witcher in particular, we had to
focus on things that would support the level

00:03:58.460 --> 00:03:59.880
of stunt work that I was doing."

00:03:59.880 --> 00:04:04.400
Rienzi called the Romanian deadlift the quote
"key foundation movement" of their sessions.

00:04:04.420 --> 00:04:08.000
It strengthens the glutes, hamstrings, and
the whole posterior chain.

00:04:08.000 --> 00:04:09.180
The trainer says that,

00:04:09.180 --> 00:04:13.120
"The whole key here is just maximizing time
under tension so he's able to fatigue the

00:04:13.120 --> 00:04:16.560
muscles more but not over-stress his nervous
system and his adrenals."

00:04:16.840 --> 00:04:21.420
In June 2017, Cavill shared a throwback photo
with his Instagram followers, giving them

00:04:21.430 --> 00:04:23.630
a look inside his training for The Witcher.

00:04:23.630 --> 00:04:28.000
The actor became a regular at Budapest's Flex
Gym while he was on location in Hungary, and

00:04:28.000 --> 00:04:30.140
the staff looked after him for the duration.

00:04:30.150 --> 00:04:33.870
The gym had everything that Cavill needed
to stay Geralt-ready, but he didn't always

00:04:33.870 --> 00:04:36.920
opt for the fanciest machine or the heaviest
weights.

00:04:36.920 --> 00:04:41.220
When he came across this old snap of himself
lifting some pretty small dumbbells at Flex,

00:04:41.220 --> 00:04:44.520
Cavill decided to share a little pearl of
workout wisdom with the world.

00:04:44.520 --> 00:04:47.380
"It doesn't take huge weights everyday to
achieve results.

00:04:47.389 --> 00:04:51.590
I was doing everything I could in a busy busy
schedule to try and get something in, whenever

00:04:51.590 --> 00:04:52.280
I could.

00:04:52.280 --> 00:04:56.180
During this period I learned that it's not
the weight that matters, it's the workout."

00:04:56.180 --> 00:05:00.410
Cavill went on to encourage people who aren't
necessarily blessed with a frame like his,

00:05:00.410 --> 00:05:04.760
telling his fans not to be discouraged by
all the gym rats who lift massive weights.

00:05:04.760 --> 00:05:05.560
He says,

00:05:05.560 --> 00:05:08.300
"You do your weights, just make every workout
count.

00:05:08.300 --> 00:05:12.680
You might end up looking better than the fella
or lady next to you that's using those heavy weights."

00:05:13.140 --> 00:05:17.620
While training for The Witcher, Cavill did
regular hyperextensions to reinforce his posterior

00:05:17.620 --> 00:05:22.340
chain and strengthen his lower back, using
a glute ham machine to make the exercise extra

00:05:22.340 --> 00:05:23.630
challenging for him.

00:05:23.630 --> 00:05:27.871
The actor did three sets of ten reps and would
hold each repetition for two seconds, all

00:05:27.880 --> 00:05:29.800
while keeping his hands behind his head.

00:05:29.800 --> 00:05:33.940
In a tutorial video for Men's Health, Cavill's
coach Dave Rienzi explained,

00:05:33.940 --> 00:05:36.930
"The focus here is again on isolating the
posterior chain.

00:05:36.930 --> 00:05:38.610
Really activating the glutes and the lower
back."

00:05:38.610 --> 00:05:42.400
It might seem odd that Cavill spent so much
time working on muscles that remain covered

00:05:42.400 --> 00:05:45.770
for the most part, but getting in shape for
The Witcher wasn't just about looking good

00:05:45.770 --> 00:05:49.700
with his clothes off, it was about making
sure he was up for major physical challenges

00:05:49.700 --> 00:05:51.140
on a daily basis.

00:05:51.140 --> 00:05:52.240
As the Brit said,

00:05:52.250 --> 00:05:55.900
"When it comes to the posterior chain and
the kind of stunts I have to do, especially

00:05:55.900 --> 00:05:59.860
when it's pirouettes with swords, anything
which is based upon one-leg movement where

00:05:59.860 --> 00:06:02.840
a knee can have a bad injury...this stuff
is what saves me."

00:06:03.480 --> 00:06:07.300
Finding time to exercise when a project is
still in pre-production is usually pretty

00:06:07.310 --> 00:06:11.080
straightforward for actors, but maintaining
an impressive physique throughout a shoot

00:06:11.080 --> 00:06:12.600
is way more challenging.

00:06:12.600 --> 00:06:16.020
That's especially true when it comes to a
long project like The Witcher.

00:06:16.020 --> 00:06:20.160
Henry Cavill told Men's Health UK that at
one particularly intense point during the

00:06:20.160 --> 00:06:21.160
production,

00:06:21.160 --> 00:06:24.080
"[We were doing] 16 and 15-hour shoot days."

00:06:24.080 --> 00:06:28.500
That meant that in order to stay in top shape,
he had to become a master of time management.

00:06:28.500 --> 00:06:32.080
The actor revealed that he was getting up
at 3 a.m. every morning so he had enough time

00:06:32.080 --> 00:06:36.560
to shower and get his extensive hair and makeup
applied before the cameras started rolling.

00:06:36.560 --> 00:06:39.340
In December 2019, he told Entertainment Tonight,

00:06:39.340 --> 00:06:42.080
"The most taxing thing is always going to
be time."

00:06:42.080 --> 00:06:43.080
He goes on to say,

00:06:43.080 --> 00:06:46.919
"It's just about getting that training in
each day and forcing yourself to do it.

00:06:46.919 --> 00:06:50.080
You've finished a very long shift and you
were there two-and-a-half hours early for

00:06:50.080 --> 00:06:52.800
your hair and your makeup, and then you have
to go to the gym."

00:06:52.800 --> 00:06:57.580
In an Instagram post, Cavill's workout coach
Dave Rienzi praised the actor's dedication:

00:06:57.580 --> 00:07:01.760
"His choice to take things to the next level
is no small task as he's currently working

00:07:01.760 --> 00:07:06.120
a grueling shoot schedule...His 110 percent
commitment is no joke."

00:07:06.740 --> 00:07:10.300
Henry Cavill's shoulders have always been
pretty heroic, but the stacked actor knew

00:07:10.310 --> 00:07:12.980
he'd need them to be stronger than ever for
The Witcher.

00:07:12.980 --> 00:07:17.290
Dave Rienzi advised the A-lister to use a
combination of side laterals and front raises

00:07:17.290 --> 00:07:20.620
to make sure he was hitting all the right
spots in one exercise.

00:07:20.620 --> 00:07:24.900
During their "Train Like a Celebrity" tutorial
for Men's Health, Rienzi revealed that,

00:07:24.900 --> 00:07:27.340
"Each repetition is actually three repetitions."

00:07:27.340 --> 00:07:28.750
Rienzi goes on to say,

00:07:28.750 --> 00:07:32.729
"He's starting out in a traditional side lateral
for the first rep, then he's coming a little

00:07:32.729 --> 00:07:36.710
further forward for the next one, and then
doing a traditional front raise."

00:07:36.710 --> 00:07:41.120
Combining these exercises into one meant that
Cavill could work the medial deltoid and the

00:07:41.120 --> 00:07:45.150
anterior deltoid at the same time, giving
him the size and strength he needed to stay

00:07:45.150 --> 00:07:47.639
safe during The Witcher's intense action sequences.

00:07:47.639 --> 00:07:50.460
Cavill said of his tailored shoulder workout,

00:07:50.460 --> 00:07:53.440
"This really helps with the sword fighting
aspect."

00:07:53.440 --> 00:07:55.000
Cavill also revealed that

00:07:55.000 --> 00:07:58.370
"When you're film fighting, you're not going
through for kill strikes, you're pulling the

00:07:58.370 --> 00:08:02.120
blow at the last second, but you have to keep
that speed up between the striking moment

00:08:02.120 --> 00:08:04.600
and the stopping moment to make it look realistic."

00:08:05.200 --> 00:08:10.000
Just like the rest of his workout, Henry Cavill's
dumbbell curls were tailored to his specific needs.

00:08:10.000 --> 00:08:14.380
The actor had to have forearms that were capable
of taming big, strong horses for extended

00:08:14.389 --> 00:08:15.650
periods of time.

00:08:15.650 --> 00:08:20.080
In the source material, Geralt is an experienced
rider and goes through numerous horses, all

00:08:20.080 --> 00:08:21.640
of whom he named Roach.

00:08:21.650 --> 00:08:25.900
Dave Rienzi had his client do dumbbell curls
alternating from a static hold, which helped

00:08:25.900 --> 00:08:28.340
sculpt those huge forearms you see in the
show.

00:08:28.340 --> 00:08:31.980
During his "Train Like a Celebrity" video
for Men's Health, he said that,

00:08:31.980 --> 00:08:35.500
"With horse riding also this can make a difference."

00:08:35.510 --> 00:08:36.520
He goes on to say,

00:08:36.520 --> 00:08:40.919
"If you have a particularly powerful horse,
whether it be a stallion or anything else,

00:08:40.919 --> 00:08:45.060
which is really, really going for it, to have
that necessary heave back on the bit, it does

00:08:45.060 --> 00:08:45.780
help."

00:08:45.780 --> 00:08:49.620
Having muscular endurance in the forearms
was also essential for the show's complicated

00:08:49.620 --> 00:08:50.440
swordplay.

00:08:50.440 --> 00:08:54.320
According to Cavill, just hanging onto his
sword is enough of a challenge come the end

00:08:54.320 --> 00:08:55.600
of a long day of shooting.

00:08:55.600 --> 00:08:56.400
He says,

00:08:56.400 --> 00:08:59.760
"When you're holding a sword, the first few
takes are fine."

00:08:59.760 --> 00:09:00.970
But he makes a point to mention,

00:09:00.970 --> 00:09:05.540
"When you're into take 16 of the day and you're
doing very complex movements with your wrist,

00:09:05.540 --> 00:09:09.200
your forearm does start to die, and you end
up throwing swords across the room rather

00:09:09.200 --> 00:09:10.460
than making a swing."

00:09:10.460 --> 00:09:14.870
Luckily, Cavill put the work in, and no one
in the cast was ever impaled by a flying sword,

00:09:14.870 --> 00:09:16.700
at least as far as we know.

00:09:17.200 --> 00:09:20.860
The Witcher has more than its fair share of
fight scenes, and many of them had to be filmed

00:09:20.860 --> 00:09:22.170
several times over.

00:09:22.170 --> 00:09:26.160
When you're working on a set piece for a show
as large as this one, there are so many variables

00:09:26.160 --> 00:09:26.660
involved.

00:09:27.020 --> 00:09:31.260
Choreography has to be nailed down, the pulled-blows
have to look convincing, and there's often

00:09:31.260 --> 00:09:33.140
a load of extras to organize.

00:09:33.140 --> 00:09:37.220
That means a fight sequence will rarely be
pulled off in one take, something Cavill was

00:09:37.220 --> 00:09:39.600
aware of well before going into The Witcher.

00:09:39.600 --> 00:09:43.640
To make sure he was ready to go at it all
day long, Cavill and Dave Rienzi dedicated

00:09:43.640 --> 00:09:45.560
a lot of time to his core strength.

00:09:45.560 --> 00:09:49.580
Cavill's coach had him doing a tweaked version
of the oblique static hold, extending his

00:09:49.580 --> 00:09:53.740
arms outwards and holding for 30 seconds before
going into extensions.

00:09:53.740 --> 00:09:54.940
According to Rienzi,

00:09:54.950 --> 00:09:58.820
"Basically what this is allowing us to do
is activate the transverse abdominals and

00:09:58.820 --> 00:10:00.280
the obliques at the same time."

00:10:00.280 --> 00:10:04.440
That helps bolster endurance, something Cavill
needed to in order to swing around a sword

00:10:04.440 --> 00:10:05.620
for hours on end.

00:10:05.620 --> 00:10:07.920
In his Men's Health tutorial, Cavill said,

00:10:07.920 --> 00:10:12.260
"If I'm using a real weighted sword it's very
heavy and requires lots of endurance to do

00:10:12.270 --> 00:10:17.130
the moves safely and perfectly each time and
it also allows for nice explosive movement,

00:10:17.130 --> 00:10:18.790
which is very typical for The Witcher."

00:10:18.790 --> 00:10:22.510
In short, Cavill's efforts to get into shape
for The Witcher have been nothing short of

00:10:22.510 --> 00:10:23.520
legendary.

